 "title": "Improving AI Discernment",
 "authors": [
  "Yamil R. Velez"
 ],
 "summary": "A US online-panel survey experiment (raw N = 2,257; analysis N = 2,030) randomised participants to eleven interventions or a no-intervention control (n = 181) and measured accuracy at classifying real versus AI-generated items. The study was not pre-registered, so every test is post hoc; no multiple-testing correction was applied. Pooled across arms, total accuracy was not distinguishable from control (+0.010, SE 0.007, p = 0.132, two-sided). Automated Flagging (+0.044, p = 0.004) and AI Literacy Guide (+0.047, p = 0.043) scored above control on total accuracy; Mindfulness scored below (-0.039, p = 0.032). For AI-generated items the pooled effect was +0.038 (p = 0.0004, two-sided), with the Breathing Exercise, AI Accuracy Nudge and AI Literacy Guide arms above control. For real items, only",
 "created": "2026-10-01",
